{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch44nwZqUnRNzqx1zTshR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"- **Context:** `go vet ./...` came back clean. `doc.go` describes a pure drawing package: a pipeline box on the left, agent events on the right, and no disk reads. `.golangci.yml` enables `funlen`, `gocyclo` (threshold 15) and `lll`.\n- **Most important, `gocyclo`:** Rendering code branches on step state, terminal width, truncation, wrapping and empty or overflow cases. Those branches pile up in a single draw function, and each combination needs its own test. Capping complexity at 15 pushes that logic into small, separately testable helpers.\n- **Second, `funlen`:** Layout code tends to grow into long, sequential \"draw everything\" functions even when each branch is simple, so it catches a different problem than `gocyclo`. Short functions keep the left-box and right-events panes composable, which suits a library that only draws what the caller gives it. `lll` is mostly cosmetic, so I ranked it last."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":490,"cache_read_input_tokens":19139,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":490},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed066545-3508-488d-8ed1-3e24880e607a","uuid":"81e5d753-1c0f-4b87-9baf-15fa9fa8e049","timestamp":"2026-11-15T04:15:55.682Z","request_id":"req_011Ch44nwQAbWufUYtMz3Riw"}
